<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.FoldersCard">
  <!-- Three settings rows: an icon, a title + secondary line, the controls trailing, and — on the two
       folder rows — a live path (and, for 数据文件夹, its kind and size) on the expansion row below. See
       the "row spec's shared classes" block in Themes/Shell/Launcher.axaml for the anatomy, and
       AppearanceCard's code-behind for the full ReloadFromConfig contract every settings card group
       follows (and for why every row here is a Grid and never a DockPanel).

       WHY THE PATH LINES ARE NOT IN THE HEADER. They used to be a third (and, on 数据文件夹, a fourth)
       TextBlock inside the Grid.Column="1" stack, which is what put that row's icon 28.33 DIP below
       where every other row's icon sat: the icon centres on the header block, and that block was twice
       the height it is anywhere else. They are value lines, so they go on the expansion row, and they
       carry tm-card-value. The class is also what stopped them floating in mid-card, which is the defect
       the user screenshotted: an unstated HorizontalAlignment plus a MaxWidth centres a line in Avalonia
       (ArrangeCore runs Stretch through Center's arithmetic), and the two lines measured 384.67 and
       456.67 DIP right of their own titles. They now start on their title's own x. The MaxWidth that
       provoked it is GONE — re-measured on the spanning expansion row these lines now sit on and found
       to bound nothing there, so it was deleted rather than inherited; see tm-card-value's own remark in
       Launcher.axaml for the floor measurement that settled it. Trimming still applies when the row
       genuinely runs out, and the code-behind sets a matching ToolTip on both path lines so the full
       text stays one hover away.

       WHY ALL THREE BUTTONS TRAIL, INCLUDING ON 数据文件夹 AND 维护. Until Round 5 they sat on their own
       full-width row below, because three buttons sharing column 2 with a column 1 that ALSO held a
       260 DIP NoWrap path line were measured to clip past the visible edge at the app's documented
       minimum window width. With the path lines off the header that
       premise is gone, and the measurement was retaken rather than inherited: the live window was shrunk
       with SetWindowPos until the platform clamped it at its enforced minimum (then MainWindow.axaml's
       MinWidth="760"; GetWindowRect 1162 px = 760 DIP client + the 22 px horizontal inset), and every
       button on the page was read from its UIA rect. Nothing clips. Round 7, Task 8 widened the
       navigation pane from 48 to 160 DIP and moved that MinWidth to 872 BY THE SAME 112 DIP, precisely so
       this measurement would keep holding: what the buttons actually sit in is the CONTENT PANE, and
       872 − 161 of chrome is the same 711 DIP as 760 − 49 was. The premise below is therefore an 872 DIP
       window with a 711 DIP content pane, and every figure taken at the old floor is unchanged.
       On both rows the three-button strip ends exactly on the card's content right
       edge, with the standard 12 DIP gutter to the text column, and it does so in English too — the
       worse case, where 重置为默认 (104.67 DIP) becomes Reset to Default (133.33). So the row spec needs
       no "three or more go below" exception: controls trail, full-width content goes below, and 主文件夹
       and 数据文件夹 are finally the same shape.

       What the floor does cost is wrapping, and HOW MUCH IS A FUNCTION OF THE CONFIGURED FONT, not a
       constant of the page. MEASURED at 150 % on the shipped build, UIA on DataFolderSub at the 872 DIP
       floor, WITH THE APP'S DEFAULT FONT (general.fontFamily = "", i.e. AppFonts.UiStack): 数据文件夹's
       subtitle takes TWO rendered lines in Chinese (410 DIP wide, 32.67 tall against a 25 px single-line
       box) and TWO in English (364.67 wide, 32 tall against a 24 px line). With 字体 = Verdana the same
       English line takes THREE (339.33 wide, 44 tall, 66 px against a 22 px line) — so no single count
       belongs in this comment without the font it was taken at. That is not the buttons' doing and
       moving them would not fix the page — at the same width, default font, English, 每列个数's subtitle
       wraps to two lines with nothing but a 220 DIP ComboBox beside it (ColCountSub 393.33 DIP wide,
       31.33 tall), and 主文件夹's wraps to two with only two buttons (MainFolderSub 480.67 wide, 32
       tall). tm-card-sub wraps on purpose; a wrapped header is a property of the width the app actually
       opens at and of the face it is set in, not of any button placement. -->
  <HeaderedContentControl Classes="tm-group-box" Theme="{StaticResource GroupBox}">
    <HeaderedContentControl.Header>
      <TextBlock x:Name="GroupHead" Classes="tm-group-head" />
    </HeaderedContentControl.Header>
    <StackPanel>

      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE8B7;" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock x:Name="MainFolderTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="MainFolderSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Classes="tm-card-actions">
            <Button x:Name="OpenRootBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnOpenRootClick" />
            <Button x:Name="PickRootBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnPickRootClick" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                      Classes="tm-card-expander tm-card-values">
            <TextBlock x:Name="RootPathText" Classes="tm-card-sub tm-card-value" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE8B7;" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock x:Name="DataFolderTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="DataFolderSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Classes="tm-card-actions">
            <Button x:Name="OpenDataBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnOpenDataClick" />
            <Button x:Name="ChangeDataBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnChangeDataClick" />
            <Button x:Name="ResetDataBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnResetDataClick" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                      Classes="tm-card-expander tm-card-values">
            <TextBlock x:Name="DataPathText" Classes="tm-card-sub tm-card-value" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="DataInfoText" Classes="tm-card-sub tm-card-value" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE74D;" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock x:Name="MaintenanceTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="MaintenanceSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Classes="tm-card-actions">
            <Button x:Name="ClearCacheBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnClearCacheClick" />
            <Button x:Name="BackupBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnBackupConfigClick" />
            <Button x:Name="RestoreBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnRestoreConfigClick" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>
    </StackPanel>
  </HeaderedContentControl>
</UserControl>
